<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Amon of Judah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">7th century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century-bce">7th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Amon was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/judah">Judah</a> for about two years in the mid-7th century BCE, the son and successor of Manasseh. The Bible says he continued his father's religious policies and was murdered by his own servants in the palace. The people of the land killed the conspirators and placed his eight-year-old son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/josiah">Josiah</a> on the throne.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/amon-of-judah.jpg" alt="Amon of Judah" width="320" height="318" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Published by Guillaume Rouillé (1518?-1589) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Amon_rex.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
